{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QWKMDjnNMsvwXUCEoUSgwy","type":"tool_result","content":"{\"result\":\"{\\\"answer\\\":\\\"Based on my search of the context filesystem, I can answer your question:\\\\n\\\\nThe cluster ID field in the ClusterIdRecord metadata record is defined as **String** type.\\\\n\\\\nThis decision emerged from the KIP-1262 (Enable auto-formatting directories) discussion threads. Initially, Jun Rao suggested making it UUID type to maintain consistency with TopicRecord's topicId field. However, Kevin Wu argued for keeping it as String type based on backward compatibility concerns:\\\\n\\\\n> \\\\\\\"Currently, you can format a cluster with a non-UUID cluster ID string, and kafka considers this 'well-formatted'... many places in kafka broker/controller code (e.g. the raft client, broker lifecycle manager, and even the formatter itself) only require this type to be a String. Since not all Strings are valid UUIDs, making this record field of type UUID might be too restrictive and complicate upgrading the MV for existing clusters, since they might have a non-UUID cluster id string, but need to write this record when upgrading to an MV that supports this feature.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\nAfter reading this explanation, Jun Rao agreed with Kevin Wu's position, stating: \\\\\\\"Thanks for the reply. The KIP looks good to me now.\\\\\\\"\\\\n\\\\n**Source files:**\\\\n- `/store/events/2026/03/03/mail-83ad205748b8bcc48f38fbfa-9d60f969.md`\\\\n- `/store/events/2026/03/03/mail-1b0d288656e30ec27f44de4f-1e1b9644.md`\\\\n- `/store/events/2026/02/18/mail-2d2cdd9e66fc4758f70d714c-35b213a8.md`\\\",\\\"error\\\":null,\\\"files\\\":[\\\"store\\\",\\\"events/2026/02/18/github-api-apache-kafka-pr-21507-opened-c44dd625.md\\\",\\\"events/2026/02/18/mail-2d2cdd9e66fc4758f70d714c-35b213a8.md\\\",\\\"events/2026/02/18/mail-979d019b1a7020acae3fdd3c-b3a0dafa.md\\\",\\\"events/2026/03/12/mail-7a7cdc92294ddcab3d2bd9ce-851f814d.md\\\",\\\"event